You are a senior product designer and front-end engineer. Your job is to REDESIGN AND REFINE THE VISUAL LAYER of the existing Konnekt codebase (Phase 0 and Phase 1 are built and working) so every screen looks like a polished, premium, modern social app. The current UI is functionally correct but visually rough: tight spacing, weak hierarchy, plain solid bars, unstyled poll and question posts, initials-only avatars with no character, murky dark mode, and a feed filled with test data. Fix all of it.

Konnekt is a verified-students-only social PWA for Nigerian universities. Users are mostly students on budget Android phones with weak, expensive data. The look is: friendly, calm, modern campus life. Not corporate, not noisy.

=== 1. HARD RULES ===
- Change ONLY the presentation layer: components, styles, layout, icons, illustrations, microcopy, motion. Do NOT change the data model, APIs, auth, audience/visibility logic, permissions, rate limits, offline/outbox logic or business rules.
- All existing tests must keep passing. If a selector changes, update the test, never weaken it. Keep roles, labels and test ids.
- Keep Next.js, Tailwind and the Phase 0 token architecture; improve the tokens centrally and make every screen consume them. No hard-coded colours in components.
- Keep performance: no new heavy dependencies (anything added must be under 15 KB gzipped; prefer inline SVG and CSS). Self-host fonts with next/font (Plus Jakarta Sans 500/600/700 for headings, Inter 400/500/600 for body, latin subset, font-display swap, system-font fallback). Keep Lighthouse mobile slow-4G budgets: Performance >= 90, Accessibility >= 95. No layout shift: reserve aspect ratios for all media.
- Do not add features. Do not ask me questions. Make the most refined choice and document it in docs/UI-REFINEMENT.md.

=== 2. MANDATORY WORKING LOOP (this is how you avoid ugly results) ===
You must LOOK at the UI, not assume.
1. Build a screenshot harness (pnpm shots) with Playwright that renders EVERY screen and state listed in section 8, in light AND dark mode, at 390x844 (mobile) and, for admin and wide layouts, 1440x900. Save to design/review/<screen>-<mode>-<viewport>.png.
2. Open and view each screenshot with your image viewing ability. For each, write down concrete defects against the rubric in section 9.
3. Fix, re-shoot, re-view. Repeat until every screen passes the rubric in both modes. Do at least three full passes over the main screens (Pulse feed, composer, post detail, profile, onboarding, admin queue).
4. Do not declare done on the basis of code reading or passing tests. Done means you have looked at the final screenshots and they look good.
5. Commit in logical steps (tokens, components, shell, each screen group). Write docs/UI-REFINEMENT.md with before/after notes and any deviations.

