=== 5B. STYLE PLACEMENT MAP (which visual style goes where) ===
Six styles are allowed, and each ONLY in the places listed. They all share the same tokens (colours, fonts, radius scale, icon set); a style only changes the surface treatment inside its zone.
1. FLAT + MATERIAL 3 EXPRESSIVE: the base for about 85% of the app. Everything not listed below is flat with solid surfaces, 1px borders and strong contrast.
2. FROSTED GLASS: only the top bar, bottom tab bar, bottom sheets (create, post menus, report, share, audience picker), the controls floating over images in the image viewer, and text overlaid on cover images. Never on cards, comments, forms, tables or admin screens.
3. SKEUOMORPHISM (small real-world touches only): (a) the Create button, slightly raised and pressable; (b) a compact ID-card-style “Verified student” card on profiles: 72 high, 12 radius, thin accent stripe on the left, small university crest, name, “Verified student · Software Engineering 300L · Nova University” (never show the matric number publicly); (c) rubber-stamp status marks (Approved, Pending, Rejected: slightly rotated, bordered, uppercase, slight ink texture) on the verification result screens and in the admin verification detail. Ticket-shaped cards are reserved for the events phase and are not built now. Never on backgrounds, lists, navigation or text areas.
4. NEO-BRUTALISM (loud moments only): the primary button on the Welcome screen and the “Open in Konnekt” button on the public share preview page: 2px dark border, hard 4px offset shadow, saturated accent or amber blocks, high-contrast label. Never on the feed, comments, forms, settings, messaging, admin or any sensitive space. One neo-brutalist block per screen at most.
5. CLAYMORPHISM (illustrations and avatars only): empty, error, pending, success and not-available illustrations, the onboarding hero, and default avatars (soft rounded forms, gentle gradients, subtle inner highlights, never glossy). Never on buttons, inputs, cards or text containers.
6. NEVER USE ANYWHERE: neumorphism (soft extruded or inset shadows), Apple Liquid Glass imitation (refraction, lensing, specular glows), dark gradients, glossy 3D buttons, heavy shadows, textured backgrounds, photorealistic faces.
LIMIT: any one screen has the flat base, the glass chrome, and at most ONE accent style (a skeuomorphic touch, a neo-brutalist block, or a clay illustration). The only exception is the Welcome screen, which may combine its neo-brutalist button with a clay hero illustration.
PER-SCREEN MAP:
- Welcome: flat + neo-brutalist button + clay hero. Public share preview: flat + neo-brutalist button.
- Find university, create account, login, forgot and reset password, settings, legal pages, composer, post detail, comments: flat only (plus glass sheets where sheets appear).
- Verification method, email, code and ID upload: flat. Verification waiting: flat + clay hourglass. Verification approved and rejected: flat + stamp (no illustration).
- Pulse feed, drafts, bookmarks, hashtag page: flat + glass top and tab bars + raised Create button; empty and error states use clay illustrations.
- Menus, report, share, audience picker: glass bottom sheets. Delete confirmation: flat dialog. Image viewer: glass controls over black.
- Profiles: flat + glass bars + the ID-card-style Verified student card.
- Blocked and muted: flat; its empty state is clay. Removed post: flat. Post not available: flat + clay envelope.
- All admin consoles: flat only (no glass, no skeuomorphism, no neo-brutalism); clay only inside empty states.

=== 6. POST CARD (the most important component) ===
Layout (16 padding, 12 gap between rows):
- Header row: avatar 48 at left; to its right a stacked block: name 16/22 600 with verified badge inline, then “@handle · 1h ago” 14/20 secondary; a three-dot icon button (44x44 hit area) at far right.
- Audience line directly under the header, aligned with the name: a 14px people icon + “to My Level · Software Engineering 300L” 13/18 secondary (text-secondary, icon tertiary). Public posts show a globe icon and “to Public · Nova University”.
- Body: 16/24 text-primary, hashtags and @mentions in accent 500, links underlined accent, collapsed after 6 lines with a “Read more” accent link.
- Media: 12 radius, 1px border, lazy loaded, aspect ratios reserved. One image: full card width, max height 360, object-fit cover. Two: side by side 1:1 with 2px gap. Three: one large left 2:3 and two stacked right. Four: 2x2. Tap opens the viewer. A “+N” overlay when more than four.
- Action row: four equal columns (comment, repost, heart, bookmark), each icon 20 + count 13/18 secondary with 6px gap, 44 high. Heart active = danger red filled with a pop animation. Repost active = success green. Bookmark active = accent filled. Counts hidden when zero (icon only), abbreviated above 999 (1.2k).
Question variant: 3px accent left border on the card (the card keeps its radius), a “Question” chip (accent-tint fill, accent text, help-circle icon, 12/16 600) above the body, an “Answered” green chip once an answer is accepted, and a small outlined “I can help” button (32 high, accent) aligned right on the body baseline.
Poll variant: a “Poll” chip with a bar-chart icon; each option is a 44 high rounded 12 row. Before voting: outlined rows with an empty radio. After voting or when ended: a background fill bar in accent-tint (the voted option in accent at 22% with a check icon and bold label), percentage right-aligned 14/20 600 tabular numbers, then “312 votes · 2 days left” in caption secondary. Bars animate width in 400 ms.
Repost variant: a “Ngozi reposted” line with a repeat icon above the header (13/18 secondary); the original appears as a nested quoted card (surface-1 fill, 1px border, 12 radius, 12 padding, small header with avatar 32) with the same audience line. The nested card is tappable.
Edited posts show “Edited” in the caption after the time. Removed posts show a grey card with an info icon and “This post was removed by a moderator for breaking the community rules.” with a Learn more link.

