=== 9. SELF-REVIEW RUBRIC (a screen passes only if ALL are true) ===
- One clear focal point and a visible three-level hierarchy (primary, secondary, tertiary text) with no competing bold elements.
- All spacing is on the 4px grid and consistent between similar elements; nothing is cramped; no element touches an edge closer than 16px on mobile.
- Only sizes from the type scale; at most three text styles per card; long names, long posts and long hashtags truncate or wrap gracefully with no overflow.
- Radii, icon stroke and border treatments are consistent; icons align optically with text.
- Alignment is exact: avatars, names, audience lines and action columns line up across cards.
- Contrast meets WCAG AA in both modes (check text on accent, text on tints, secondary text).
- Touch targets are at least 44px; focus rings are visible; keyboard order is sensible.
- Every screen has designed loading, empty, error and offline states.
- Dark mode looks intentionally designed: layered surfaces, readable accent, no muddy tints, no pure-white text, images not glaring.
- Glass appears only on the top bar, bottom bar and bottom sheets, remains legible, and falls back to solid correctly.
- Style placement matches section 5B exactly: each style only where listed, at most one accent style per screen (Welcome excepted), and none of the banned styles (neumorphism, Liquid Glass imitation, glossy 3D, heavy shadows) anywhere.
- It looks like a premium, friendly, modern app a student would be proud to open. If a screen looks like a default template, plain form or developer prototype, it fails.
Anti-patterns to remove: default browser controls, unstyled inputs, random greys, inconsistent radii, tiny tap targets, cramped cards, text-only polls, plain initials avatars where an illustrated avatar belongs, loud saturated backgrounds behind reading content, shadows everywhere, and any leftover test data.

